      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Multiplication and Division from left to right:**\n   - First, we perform the multiplication \\(6 \\cdot 2\\):\n     \\[\n     6 \\cdot 2 = 12\n     \\]\n     So the expression now is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\n     \\]\n\n   - Next, we perform the multiplication \\(5 \\cdot 4\\):\n     \\[\n     5 \\cdot 4 = 20\n     \\]\n     So the expression now is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 - 3 + 20 \\div 2\n     \\]\n\n   - Then, we perform the division \\(20 \\div 2\\):\n     \\[\n     20 \\div 2 = 10\n     \\]\n     So the expression now is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 - 3 + 10\n     \\]\n\n2. **Addition and Subtraction from left to right:**\n   - First, we perform the addition \\(1 + 12\\):\n     \\[\n     1 + 12 = 13\n     \\]\n     So the expression now is:\n     \\[\n     13 - 3 + 10\n     \\]\n\n   - Next, we perform the subtraction \\(13 - 3\\):\n     \\[\n     13 - 3 = 10\n     \\]\n     So the expression now is:\n     \\[\n     10 + 10\n     \\]\n\n   - Finally, we perform the addition \\(10 + 10\\):\n     \\[\n     10 + 10 = 20\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
